new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6c692ac8c913076c4626870cc66fec7ba4442424
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fixture/runs/f2/RETIRED.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+Run f2: 16/18 checks passed, then RETIRED (NOT counted). Both failures were DRIVER expectations, not product behaviour.
+- I: C2 sends Content-Length with the response head; when the download then fails ("not enough shards: 9/10") it closes
+  the connection with a SHORT body (sia-s3 src/s3.rs: "the only honest signal left is a short body"). The driver's helper
